Now app-actions: bind palette, route hashchange, copy link, ops refresh, auto-refresh, sync meta updates, boot route apply.

First loadSnapshot set syncMeta. In loadSnapshot finally? Set after success/fallback. Add after `} finally` or before loadConnections:
```
syncMeta.snapshotAt = Date.now();
```
even fallback marks attempt. Good.
- syncGitHub success set syncMeta.githubAt = Date.now(); call renderSyncStatus? In app-missions. We can add there.
- syncTrello success set syncMeta.trelloAt.
- `refreshLiveSources` in app-actions. Need not call loadSnapshot repeatedly if sourceMode fallback? Could still fetch.
Implementation:
```
async function refreshLiveSources(show=false) {
 if (syncMeta.refreshing) return false;
 syncMeta.refreshing = true;
 if (currentView==='home') renderOpsHealth();
 try {
   await loadSnapshot(); // sets state and connections
   renderAll();
   if (navigator.onLine) {
      const stale = ts => !ts || Date.now()-ts > 240000;
      if (stale(syncMeta.githubAt)) await syncGitHub(show);
      if (connections.trelloKey && ... && stale(syncMeta.trelloAt)) await syncTrello(show);
   }
   renderAll(); // re-render after sync? sync functions already render partial, but sidebar. okay
   if (show) toast('Estado actualizado');
   return true;
 } catch { if (show) toast('No se pudo actualizar'); return false; }
 finally { syncMeta.refreshing=false; renderSyncStatus(); }
}
```
But `loadSnapshot` sets `sourceMode` and `connections`; it doesn't reset localRequests? loadConnections does. Fine.
Potential issue `renderAll()` re-renders while a detail sheet open. Sheet content not re-rendered; but not closed. Fine.
Potential issue `renderAll` calls renderWorld which calls syncWorldLive and uses state; okay.
Potential issue if `syncGitHub` already in progress not tracked; okay.
- Auto-refresh timer:
```
function startAutoRefresh() {
 clearInterval(syncMeta.timer);
 syncMeta.timer = setInterval(() => {
   if (document.visibilityState !== 'visible' || !navigator.onLine) return;
   if (document.querySelector('dialog[open]:not(#detailSheet)')) return;
   if (syncMeta.refreshing) return;
   refreshLiveSources(false);
 }, 60000);
 document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
   if (document.visibilityState==='visible' && (!syncMeta.snapshotAt || Date.now()-syncMeta.snapshotAt>60000)) refreshLiveSources(false);
 });
}
```
- Boot: after render and sync timeouts, start auto refresh. Also route apply:
```
async function boot() {
 hydrateIcons(); bindEvents(); loadConnections(); renderAll();
 await loadSnapshot();
 renderAll(); updateReplayUI();
 if (!location.hash) { appliedHash = routeHash('home'); history.replaceState(null,'',appliedHash); }
 applyRouteFromHash(true);
 ...
 startAutoRefresh();
}
```
But `applyRouteFromHash(true)` calls navigate -> renderHome etc again. Fine. Need it after load. If hash detail, opens sheet.
- `bindEvents` add:
  - `window.addEventListener('hashchange', () => applyRouteFromHash());`
  - `$('#opsRefresh')?.addEventListener('click', () => refreshLiveSources(true));`
  - delegated `[data-copy-link]` click -> copyCurrentLink.
  - `bindPalette();` call inside bindEvents or boot. Since app-command loaded before actions, call `bindPalette()`.
  - Maybe command palette `copyCurrentLink` declared in command file. Fine.
- `submitSettings`: after save sync meta will update; call renderOpsHealth maybe. Not needed.
- On `clearConnections`: reset syncMeta? maybe preserve snapshot; set githubAt/trelloAt null. Then renderSyncStatus. Fine.
- `renderAll` maybe call `renderOpsHealth` via renderHome only. If current view not home, ops not updated. `renderSyncStatus` in finally updates home if current view. good.
- `syncGitHub` render calls `renderSidebar` only; if currentView home, home issues update. It doesn't call renderOpsHealth. Add in syncGitHub after success/failure `renderSyncStatus()`. But `renderSyncStatus` defined app-actions loaded after missions; at runtime available. Use `if (typeof renderSyncStatus === 'function') renderSyncStatus();`. Same in syncTrello.
- Also set syncMeta in cached path? If cached, set `syncMeta.githubAt = cached.data.updatedAt || cached.time` and renderSyncStatus. `cached.data.updatedAt` is time of fetch. Good.
- `syncTrello` show error doesn't update. Fine.
- Make `renderOpsHealth` update `#opsAutoLabel` with refreshing. At start of refresh call renderOpsHealth if home.

